  "scientific_limits": [
    "NAVSIM current G1/G3 share a five-epoch perception preparation unavailable to historical S/A/V; equal driving updates do not mean equal total compute or exposure.",
    "New architecture, losses, optimizer groups and execution differ from historical S/A/V; comparisons describe overall systems, not sole auxiliary-task causal effects.",
    "G0 and G2 have not started, so G1-G0 and G3-G2 causal comparisons are unavailable.",
    "nuScenes only six-epoch G1/G3 is currently a matched completed endpoint; longer G3 results are within-run learning evidence, not a fair G1 contrast.",
    "nuScenes collision is locked UniAD-style open-loop raster box overlap, not NAVSIM responsibility collision or closed-loop safety.",
    "Historical best full Navtest values must not be compared numerically with current development results.",
    "Deployment latency measurements are cost-only engineering benchmarks, not an endpoint quality/latency tradeoff."
  ],
  "interpretation": [
    "NAVSIM G1 has a positive 25k overall-system signal against S0; G3 has not improved on G1 or historical V_QUERY at this observation.",
    "G3 reduces fixed logged GT-body local errors while lowering global occupancy IoU and event precision; local representation improvements have not yet yielded better aggregate planning.",
    "nuScenes matched six-epoch G3 has worse final collision and slightly worse three-second L2 than G1; its own 6/12/18-epoch L2 trend improves, without monotonic collision improvement.",
